:6,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":1,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":6,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{"material":6}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":95,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Cycle 132 is closed, and it produced no new VI. The second half of the slot writes (P3b-2) never reached its trial run, because the step that re-binds its plan to the real graph of the current work VI stopped three times on three different tool gaps. The work VI `D1_ring_p3b1_20261002_060910.vi` is unchanged, and LabVIEW ran only once, for a read-only graph read.\n\n**Built and self-tested:**\n- **Memory check:** it now includes the cost of the final full read of the VI. It predicts 680.8 MB for P3b-1 against the 680.4 MB measured, and the failure limit is now 690 MB. Read-only scripts are no longer refused as \"unmeasured\" (that was a wrong refusal, now fixed).\n- **Tunnel-name check:** after each step that crosses a Flat Sequence border, the new tunnel's name is compared with the simulator's prediction. Names of tunnels between frames are still not checked.\n- **Expected Error List for P3b-2:** computed by a script instead of typed: 50 to 52 items.\n- **Wrong gate refusals:** 3 of the 5 queued (fp-19, fp-20, fp-29) are fixed. fp-21 is still open, and fp-28 waits for a \"close\" command in `gate_fp.py`.\n- **Graph read of P3b-1:** the image-out and error-out wires match the simulation, with no ends swapped. That settles the open point from cycle 131.\n- **Plan re-binding tool, three gaps closed:**\n  - Terminals are now matched by their wiring, not by name. The unbundle's `status` output matches the terminal wired to `Select`.\n  - The Flat Sequence frame map is carried over from the simulated plan.\n  - A failed re-binding no longer overwrites the plan file.\n\n**Still blocking P3b-2:** after step 24 of 39, the check that compares simulated against real object IDs cannot match a tunnel created inside the Flat Sequence that P3b-1 made. The re-simulation itself completes all 39 steps.\n\n**Problems the retrospective found:**\n- **One fault, 9 minutes lost (`wrong-ordering`):** I sent the graph-read card out alongside the card that was editing the gate that read needed, so two of the six dispatches came back blocked. New rule PD281(a): a LabVIEW card follows any card that edits its pre-check tools, never runs beside it.\n- **Memory may be over the limit:** P3b-1 measured 584.1 MB just after loading, but the memory prediction still assumes a 570.0 MB start. With the measured start, P3b-2 comes out near 695.8 MB, over the 690 MB limit.\n- **Plan not finalized:** the rebuilt P3b-2 plan has the same 39 actions as the old one but is not marked final. One of this cycle's tool edits may have caused that.\n\n**Next cycle (133):** the first act is to recompute the memory prediction with the measured 584.1 MB start. If it is still above 690 MB, P3b-2 would have to be split again into a third part, which needs your decision, and the cycle stops to ask you. Otherwise it closes the step-24 matching gap and checks all 39 steps. If that cannot be closed in one card, the P3b-2 plan is built directly on the real graph instead. Then come the trial run on a copy and one real build.\n\nNo new questions for you this cycle. One older question is still open: D-2026-10-02-01, a check that stops a helper agent from finishing while its own LabVIEW run is still going.\n\nThe decisions are PD275–281 in `docs/d1/tooling.md` and `docs/d1/ring-p3b.md`, with one-line links in `docs/d1/INDEX.md`.","ttft_ms":2173,"type":"result","duration_ms":4755712,"uuid":"0e5ad108-19c6-4f46-b618-9c670565655a","ttft_stream_ms":1778,"time_to_request_ms":242,"first_content_frame_ms":1778,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
